---
/**
 * Surge versus boost — the public adjudication table.
 *
 * The table is generated from the database so a later peak_is_surge or
 * source_quote edit shows up here on the next build. Empty quotes are omitted
 * rather than faked. Discontinued records are listed separately and are not
 * on the 90-day recheck clock.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import db from '../../data/power-stations.json';
import { site } from '../../data/site.ts';
import {
  isCurrent,
  isVerificationStale,
  recheckOn,
  sourceQuoteOf,
} from '../../lib/catalog.ts';

const current = db.stations.filter(isCurrent);
const retired = db.stations.filter((s) => !isCurrent(s));
const surge = current.filter((s) => s.peak_is_surge !== false);
const boost = current.filter((s) => s.peak_is_surge === false);
const quoted = current.filter((s) => sourceQuoteOf(s)).length;

const origin = Astro.site ?? site.url;
const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Inverter surge versus boost ratings',
  description:
    'Which portable power station peak figures are inverter surge, and which are resistive boost ratings that do not clear a motor start. Each row cites the manufacturer page and the date it was read.',
  url: new URL('/guides/surge-vs-boost/', origin).href,
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: site.name },
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: site.publisherName },
};

function formatW(n: number) {
  return `${n.toLocaleString('en-US')} W`;
}
---

<Base
  title="Inverter surge versus boost ratings"
  description="X-Boost, Power Lifting, and SurgePad are resistive boost figures, not inverter surge. Each verified model is listed with the manufacturer wording and the date that page was read."
  canonicalPath="/guides/surge-vs-boost/"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Inverter surge versus boost ratings</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      A portable power station publishes two output numbers: continuous watts, and a higher peak.
      The peak is only useful against a motor if it is an inverter surge rating. Several
      manufacturers instead publish a boost figure for resistive loads (heaters, kettles, some
      tools), labelled X-Boost, Power Lifting, SurgePad, or similar. That number is stored in this
      database, and it is not used to decide whether a fridge compressor will start.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Why the difference matters</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      A compressor or a circular saw draws a brief inrush several times its running wattage. The
      inverter has to survive that instant. A resistive boost path is a different circuit: it can
      raise the ceiling for a heater without describing how the inverter behaves against a motor.
      Treating the two as the same produces a confidently wrong recommendation on exactly the load
      that gets a unit returned.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      The calculator, the refrigerator pages, and the scenario pages all call the same function. If
      the peak is a boost rating, a motor start is reported as unverified, not as cleared. The
      wording in the table is a short citation from the manufacturer page, not a lab measurement.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Current models, grouped by what the peak means</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">
      {surge.length} current models publish an inverter surge. {boost.length} publish a boost
      figure instead. {quoted} of {current.length} rows carry a source citation.
      Recheck is 90 days after the page was read. A stale date means the wording should be read
      again, not that the ruling is void.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold">Boost rating, not used against motor starts</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
      The calculator will not clear a compressor or a saw against these peaks.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-ink-200 dark:border-ink-800">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse bg-white text-left text-sm dark:bg-ink-900">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-ink-200 dark:border-ink-800">
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Model</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Printed peak</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Ruling</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Source wording</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Read</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Recheck</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            boost.map((s) => {
              const quote = sourceQuoteOf(s);
              const stale = isVerificationStale(s.verified_at);
              return (
                <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 last:border-0 hover:bg-ink-50 dark:border-ink-800/60 dark:hover:bg-ink-800/40">
                  <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">
                    <a href={`/stations/${s.id}/`} class="hover:text-moss-700 dark:hover:text-moss-300">
                      {s.brand} {s.model}
                    </a>
                  </th>
                  <td class="tabular px-4 py-3">{formatW(s.output_peak_w)}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3">Boost, not motor start</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3">
                    {quote ? (
                      <>
                        <span class="block">{quote}</span>
                        <a
                          href={s.source_url}
                          rel="nofollow noopener"
                          target="_blank"
                          class="mt-1 inline-block text-xs text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300"
                        >
                          Source
                        </a>
                      </>
                    ) : (
                      <span class="text-ink-500">Citation pending</span>
                    )}
                  </td>
                  <td class="tabular px-4 py-3">{s.verified_at}</td>
                  <td class:list={['tabular px-4 py-3', stale && 'text-amber-accent-700 dark:text-amber-accent-300']}>
                    {recheckOn(s.verified_at)}
                    {stale ? ' · stale' : ''}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              );
            })
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">Inverter surge, used against motor starts</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
      These peaks are checked against compressor and tool inrush. A pass is still an estimate, not
      a lab start.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-ink-200 dark:border-ink-800">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse bg-white text-left text-sm dark:bg-ink-900">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-ink-200 dark:border-ink-800">
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Model</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Printed peak</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Ruling</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Source wording</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Read</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Recheck</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            surge.map((s) => {
              const quote = sourceQuoteOf(s);
              const stale = isVerificationStale(s.verified_at);
              return (
                <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 last:border-0 hover:bg-ink-50 dark:border-ink-800/60 dark:hover:bg-ink-800/40">
                  <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">
                    <a href={`/stations/${s.id}/`} class="hover:text-moss-700 dark:hover:text-moss-300">
                      {s.brand} {s.model}
                    </a>
                  </th>
                  <td class="tabular px-4 py-3">{formatW(s.output_peak_w)}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3">Inverter surge</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3">
                    {quote ? (
                      <>
                        <span class="block">{quote}</span>
                        <a
                          href={s.source_url}
                          rel="nofollow noopener"
                          target="_blank"
                          class="mt-1 inline-block text-xs text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300"
                        >
                          Source
                        </a>
                      </>
                    ) : (
                      <span class="text-ink-500">Citation pending</span>
                    )}
                  </td>
                  <td class="tabular px-4 py-3">{s.verified_at}</td>
                  <td class:list={['tabular px-4 py-3', stale && 'text-amber-accent-700 dark:text-amber-accent-300']}>
                    {recheckOn(s.verified_at)}
                    {stale ? ' · stale' : ''}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              );
            })
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    {
      retired.length > 0 ? (
        <details class="mt-10 rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-ink-200 p-4 dark:border-ink-800">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-semibold">
            Discontinued records ({retired.length}), not on the recheck clock
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-500">
            Last read on the date shown. These rows are not rechecked. The ruling stays so an old
            station page does not silently treat a boost figure as surge.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm">
            {retired.map((s) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`/stations/${s.id}/`} class="font-medium text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300">
                  {s.brand} {s.model}
                </a>
                {' · '}
                {s.peak_is_surge === false ? 'boost' : 'inverter surge'}
                {' · '}
                {formatW(s.output_peak_w)}
                {' · read '}
                {s.verified_at}
                {sourceQuoteOf(s) ? ` · ${sourceQuoteOf(s)}` : ''}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </details>
      ) : null
    }

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Each refrigerator page restates this for one model. If a manufacturer page changes the
      wording, the ruling is updated on the next verification and the calculator follows the same
      record. Brand hubs:
      {
        ['ecoflow', 'jackery', 'bluetti', 'anker-solix'].map((slug, i, arr) => (
          <>
            <a href={`/brands/${slug}/`} class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300">
              {slug === 'anker-solix' ? 'Anker SOLIX' : slug.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + slug.slice(1)}
            </a>
            {i < arr.length - 1 ? ', ' : '.'}
          </>
        ))
      }
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
